<article class="env-lemma" id="0GRM">
  <p><a class="environment-identifier" href="/tag/0GRM">Lemma <span data-tag="0GRM">106.16.4</span>.</a> Let $B \to C$ be a ring map. If </p>
  <p><ol>
  <li><p>
the coprojections $C \to C \otimes _ B C$ are flat and 
</p>
</li><li><p>
$B \to C$ is universally injective, 
</p>
</li>
</ol></p>
  <p> then $B \to C$ is faithfully flat. </p>
</article><article class="env-proof">
    <p>
      <strong>Proof.</strong>
      The map $\mathop{\mathrm{Spec}}(C) \to \mathop{\mathrm{Spec}}(B)$ is surjective as $B \to C$ is universally injective. Thus it suffices to show that $B \to C$ is flat which follows from Descent, Theorem <a href="/tag/08XD" data-tag="08XD">35.4.25</a>. 
      <span class="qed">$\square$</span>
    </p>
</article>